# Releases

Users download **GitHub Releases**, not git tags and not a repo clone.

- A push to `main` runs `.github/workflows/release.yml`. That workflow must create a GitHub **Release** (Releases tab), never only a tag.
- Each release title is `PollenForge X.Y.Z`. Notes must have separate **macOS** and **Windows** download + install sections.
- Asset names stay:
  - `PollenForge-X.Y.Z-Mac-arm64.dmg` (Apple Silicon)
  - `PollenForge-X.Y.Z-Mac-x64.dmg` (Intel)
  - `PollenForge-X.Y.Z-Windows-Setup.exe`
- Do not tell users to open the Tags page, `git clone`, or `git pull` to update an installed app.
- Docs-only commits use `[skip release]` in the message.
- Full process: `AGENTS.md`.
